The rule-level witness is now concrete: the slice rule delegates to `reverseString`, whose recursion reverses K’s backend string units; for `🙂a🙂` it produces `"\x82\x99\x9f\xf0a\x82\x99\x9f\xf0"` instead of the unchanged Python string. The local K documentation explicitly warns that strings are incomplete beyond Latin-1. I’m inventorying every local declaration and rule and machine-checking both the candidate’s wrong Unicode result and Python’s rejected expected result.
